{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas","id":528134,"title":"Amazon and Pentex Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T15:24:56-07:00","id":528134,"title":"Amazon and Pentex Ideas","content":"So I want to run some stuff in the Amazon using Pentex as an antagonist. Thing is I've never been good at using Pentex as a villain. Something about coming up with evil corporate plots that are worse then reality and turn a profit I just can't cook up to save my life. Any help would be great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:27:40-07:00","id":528613,"title":"","content":"If it's the large scale evil plot that's giving you trouble, you don't need to have one. They can just be turning a profit like anyone else, but the methods and all-round careless corruption they inflict everywhere they turn up can be all the evil a story needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:43:29-07:00","id":528624,"title":"","content":"Here's a plot hook. Amazon recently announced it would deliver packages via drones. We all know that idea was shelved quickly but it would explain a drone R&amp;D budget in their books. Maybe they made the announcement to get in front of something. Maybe just maybe a pack discovered that an off shoot of the Amazon company (or whatever your renaming it to in your game.) is developing military grade drones for urban use getting in front of a possible bill going through congress that will allow their use on American soil. Maybe to stop the pack showing them up they made the annoucement to prevent embarrassment. Now the full might of Pentex is on the packs head as they want to silence this pack before it can cause more issues or tell too many people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T04:42:18-07:00","id":528711,"title":"","content":"He is talking about Southern America, not about ye beste internet shoppe in the world (TM)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:17:54-07:00","id":529261,"title":"","content":".....yea......I meant the big river in the jungle...but thanks....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:15:13-07:00","id":529468,"title":"","content":"I know this is just a shameless plug, but have you read <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61499/Rage-Across-The-Amazon?term=rage+acro+ama\" target=\"_blank\">Rage Across the Amazon</a>? Yes, it might be a bit dated, but I can't think of a more relevant resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T16:17:43-07:00","id":530388,"title":"","content":"I actually have some ideas to share, as there was a point when I wanted to run a game in the Amazon... I ended up running a game in Egypt, but that's a whole other story. I'll dig up my notes and get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:55:28-07:00","id":530557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=530388#post530388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have some ideas to share, as there was a point when I wanted to run a game in the Amazon... I ended up running a game in Egypt, but that's a whole other story. I'll dig up my notes and get back to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheat code! Excellent thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:23:37-07:00","id":563599,"title":"","content":"Honestly, contrary to pop imagery and stuff, i don't see as Amazon as that much of a Pentex battleground, industry is almost nonexistent, at least in the brazilian part of the Amazon that is the greater part of the rainforest, afaik.<br /> <br /> Main problems there are in the region are illegal large-scale deforestation for the sake of a variety of woods, the burning of some areas for the creation of pasture and agriculture - and some drug-trafficking &amp; plantations hidden amidst the jungle, not quite Pentex's main areas of interest/operation, that involves mining, heavy industries, prospection and other &quot;hardcore-pollution&quot; sectors, from what i remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-21-2015, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:33:14-07:00","id":563660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=563599#post563599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, contrary to pop imagery and stuff, i don't see as Amazon as that much of a Pentex battleground, industry is almost nonexistent, at least in the brazilian part of the Amazon that is the greater part of the rainforest, afaik.<br /> <br /> Main problems there are in the region are illegal large-scale deforestation for the sake of a variety of woods, the burning of some areas for the creation of pasture and agriculture - and some drug-trafficking &amp; plantations hidden amidst the jungle, not quite Pentex's main areas of interest/operation, that involves mining, heavy industries, prospection and other &quot;hardcore-pollution&quot; sectors, from what i remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but O'Tolley needs to get their beef and the soybeans they use to feed that beef from somewhere. Up until VERY recently McDonald's was infamous for using beef and soy grown on deforested former rainforest land. But activist pressure finally got to them and they pledged to<a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/sustainable-business/2015/apr/21/mcdonalds-deforestation-global-supply-chain\" target=\"_blank\"> remove suppliers that contribute</a> to loss of rainforest from their supply chain.<br /> <br /> Still, in the World of Darkness, O'tolley's is probably still at it. So here's a <a href=\"http://www.mcvideogame.com/index-eng.html\" target=\"_blank\">old subversive internet favorite </a>that sum's up O'Tolley's practices perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:45:20-07:00","id":563662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=563660#post563660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but O'Tolley needs to get their beef and the soybeans they use to feed that beef from somewhere. Up until VERY recently McDonald's was infamous for using beef and soy grown on deforested former rainforest land. But activist pressure finally got to them and they pledged to<a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/sustainable-business/2015/apr/21/mcdonalds-deforestation-global-supply-chain\" target=\"_blank\"> remove suppliers that contribute</a> to loss of rainforest from their supply chain.<br /> <br /> Still, in the World of Darkness, O'tolley's is probably still at it. So here's a <a href=\"http://www.mcvideogame.com/index-eng.html\" target=\"_blank\">old subversive internet favorite </a>that sum's up O'Tolley's practices perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would fit better, though even more so in the Central-West states, close to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantanal\" target=\"_blank\">Pantanal</a> wetlands, where pecuary industry is strongest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-21-2015, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:07:11-07:00","id":563669,"title":"","content":"If you're to follow the oWoD cannon, here are some things to keep in mind when playing a chronicle in the Amazon:<br /> <br /> 1-) The leader of the Garou in the Amazon is Golgol Fangs-First, a rank 6 Ahroun from the Get of Fenris. His right hand is Carlos Walks-the-stars, a powerful Uktena theurge who managed to negotiate a Caern from the locals.<br /> 2-) The natives of the Amazon do not like Garou or Europeans in general. They believe both of them to be wyrm spawn, evil monsters who crossed the seas to rape and pillage the apex of native american civilization(Inca,Aztec,Maraj\u00f3 in the Amazon itself). They will at best distrust any Garou they meet.<br /> 3-) The Amazon is *humongous*. Just the main rainforest is a huge green carpet of tall green trees that extends for a territory about the size of Europe. There are more unique species of mammals, birds, reptiles, insects, and fish there than anywhere else in the world. There are many ancient, mysterious things lurking there also: Mokol\u00e9 caerns that are millions of years old, semi-nomad Balam tribes that will kill anyone who trespasses into their territory, willingly or not. Huge snakes living in the Amazon river and its tributaries that are said to be over 50 feet long and capable of swallowing a garou whole in Crinos form. Many more other ancient, weird things<br /> 4-) Travel in the Amazon is done mostly by boat. There are very few roads and they are in terrible shape. The Amazon river is the 2nd longest in the world and the most volumus. It also has 6 huge tributaries, and many dozens of smaller ones. There is more fresh water in the Amazon than anywhere else in the world. In fact, nearly 1/4 of the world's fresh supply lie in the Amazon Basin. However, travel is dangerous, as Pentex patrol boats roam the area.<br /> 5-) The &quot;capital of the amazon&quot; is the town of Manaus, in northern Brazil. Most &quot;expeditions&quot; should probably start from there. There is a small kindred population in Manaus, mostly independent Lasombra and Brujah coteries. Obviously, they never leave the city.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://media.escola.britannica.com.br/eb-media/55/103655-073-F1F709E2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://media.escola.britannica.com.b...3-F1F709E2.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 06-21-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:54:08-07:00","id":563699,"title":"","content":"More Weaver than Wyrm probably, but also pretty resonant:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t2q3jQUZTis\" data-code=\"t2q3jQUZTis\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/t2q3jQUZTis/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> There's some traffic by plane - a fraction of it illegal - but the usual policy of brazilian air force is &quot;gun down anything that doesn't answer a radio call, no 2nd chances.&quot;<br /> <br /> Speaking of Marajo, there's much evidence that civilization there disappeared before the arrival of europeans explorers. The isle itself, in the mouth of the Amazon river, is about the size of Switzerland but with barely 1/40 of the population a surprisingly large number of domesticated water buffalo and stands just across from the entry port and other major capital of the rainforest, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bel%C3%A9m\" target=\"_blank\">Belem do Par\u00e1</a>.<br /> <br /> About the water buffalos in Marajo, no one is completely certain of how they ended up there, though a popular story involves a ship from southeast asia that sank in the river's mouth in the 19th century. What is a fact is that they became so endemic to the isle the local police much prefers them as transportation around the place than cars or boats.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s.glbimg.com/jo/g1/f/original/2011/07/26/bufalo11.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:27:27-07:00","id":564653,"title":"","content":"More Weaver than Wyrm probably, but also pretty resonant:<br /> <br /> Oh, Native-Americans, (&quot;\u00cdndios&quot; or &quot;Indians&quot;) will very much consider Europeans to be Wyrm-spawn. Europeans brought the Eater-of-Souls and a bunch of other shit. The Americas were pretty much Wyrm-free before the Europeans came, this is standard WW cannon and applies to all the Americas, from Canada to Patagonia.<br /> <br /> But other than that I agree with pretty much everything you said, some great ideas you added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T00:07:00-07:00","id":565069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=564653#post564653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The Americas were pretty much Wyrm-free before the Europeans came, this is standard WW cannon and applies to all the Americas, from Canada to Patagonia.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were places where the Wyrm festered. The Mound Builders who were once the kin of the Croatan fell to corruption and had to be purged. There might be other examples (blood sorcerery influenced by vampires among the Aztecs) but my memory banks are too faulty.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T09:46:04-07:00","id":565498,"title":"","content":"This is all some great stuff...didn't even think of how evil I could have O'Tooleys, here I always stick with Megadon and Endron when I go for evil corporations. Right now I have it as a mokole based game. We have an American Mokole coming down to help with things and along her way stumbles into a Wallow who's been hiding out since the first Shadow Lords popped up in the 1600. As far as they were concerned they are the last wallow (which of course they're wrong). So right now the main part of the game is her trying to talk these mokole into getting involved and actually doing something as Pentex has been slowly getting closer and the rank 5 Gathering at the Wallow is of the opinion if they just hide then they'll go away. She fears getting involved will draw attention to the wallow and result in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:49:47-07:00","id":565856,"title":"","content":"Is your American Mokole a Crowned? I still remember the write-up on Mokole, p.118 of that newly Changed Crowned Mokole who his Kinfolk look to as their only leader after they all got evicted from their land. &quot;Huddled in slums and refugee camps, The People need a hero. That's you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if that's relevant here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:17:48-07:00","id":565990,"title":"","content":"No, I know what you're talking about but no...she's a Strike actually, we have a Crowned worked out but we didn't want it to be a player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T01:19:21-07:00","id":566185,"title":"","content":"Finnaly managed to dig up my notes. I was kinda remembering they were more elaborate, but at the time I was split between an Amazon and an Egypt game, and the players picked Egypt.<br /> <br /> - Lost Caerns of the Camazotz. All of them are natural caverns, and all of them have elaborately carved stalactites and stalagmites that serve as a written record of the Camazotz. While the carvings seem indecipherable, they actually respond to the winds and/or echolocation of the Camazotz and when properly &quot;read&quot; can give a detailed account of the Camazotz, their rites and gifts, as well as the locations of their other Caerns<br /> - The idea was that there would be a rush for the Camazotz Caerns between the Garou, local Fera and a highly mystical Pentex unit. This would lead to a lot of conflict as well as the possibility that some of the Caerns may be inhabited by something horrible, or even have Camazotz who have lived there as they were way too far out of touch to be murdered horribly<br /> - Golgol Fangs First recruiting the PC's as messengers and recruiters for the War, using them to coordinate the efforts all across the Amazon, affording the PC's opportunities to meet different groups and packs, as well as stepping on the feet of the local Fera - this should lead to conflicts, but maybe even an opportunity to find respect and allies<br /> - a giant half spirit, half beast Anaconda that is revered by the locals and serves as a reluctant ally to the Fera, after being introduced to the characters as a frightening, yet effective ally, the spirit starts going more and more crazy due to the efforts of a stealthy first team that has been poisoning waters near her abode, and the characters will have to either restrain or kill it<br /> - an order of immortal blood mages awoken from their slumber by either the characters or the Pentex operatives, they seek to restore their powers, their lost artifacts and enough sacrifices to bring a permenent eclipse upon the world. The characters are helped in fighting them by their ancient enemies, who could be anything from Spirts or Wraiths to actual orders of Mummies or Mages<br /> <br /> Sorry that it wasn't more eleborate... I remember there being more stuff, but this is everything I noted down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:23:02-07:00","id":566582,"title":"","content":"I'm going to dump here some folk tales from the native <b>Tupi</b> tribes of the Amazon region, maybe it can help to flavor your chronicle:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1-) Boitat\u00e1 - A huge, anti-deluvian Anaconda(over 70feet) with fiery red eyes, capable of seeing perfectly during the night. It stalks its prey across the Amazon river and its tributaries, often turning up boats to eat those inside. It is also capable of controlling local weather to a small degree, causing storms and lightning.<br /> 2-) Curupira - An ancient forest spirit that takes the form of a human dwarf with red hair, it is said to protect the local fauna by misleading hunters and gibing them trouble by making fake animal tracks on the land. The local Tupi offered him tobacco, feathers and blankets to appease him. He has occasionally been spotted riding on top of a huge boar.<br /> 3-) Boto - This fresh water dolphin native to the Amazon is said to be capable of switching into the human form of a handsome young man, seducing women and getting them pregnant, before jumping back on the river and turning back into a dolphin. (+1 were-dolphins of the Amazon)<br /> 4-) Mapinguari - A huge monster that is said to be about 7ft tall, humanoid in shape, covered in scales, with huge razor-sharp claws and a dog's muzzle. This is like the brazillian Sasquatch, there have been numerous sights of him in the jungle and serious expeditions organized to try to identify it, but nothing conclusive has ever been found<span style=\"color:#252525\">.Accounts state that it gave off a putrid stench and emitted a frightening shriek, and that weapons such as arrows and bullets could not penetrate the Mapinguari\u2019s<br /> alligator-like hide.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 06-24-2015, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:41:21-07:00","id":567026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=566582#post566582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4-) Mapinguari - A huge monster that is said to be about 7ft tall, humanoid in shape, covered in scales, with huge razor-sharp claws and a dog's muzzle. This is like the brazillian Sasquatch, there have been numerous sights of him in the jungle and serious expeditions organized to try to identify it, but nothing conclusive has ever been found<span style=\"color:#252525\">.Accounts state that it gave off a putrid stench and emitted a frightening shriek, and that weapons such as arrows and bullets could not penetrate the Mapinguari\u2019s<br /> alligator-like hide.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mapinguari is a interesting one indeed. Though some details like fur and scales, the overpowering stench remain consistent through most descriptions, there considerable variety between descriptions depending on source and theory, its appearance going from something like a gigantic <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megatherium\" target=\"_blank\">sloth</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pangolin\" target=\"_blank\">pangolin</a> to a <a href=\"http://ahduvido.com.br/wp-content/uploads/mapinguari-lenda-amazonica.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">jungle relative</a> of lovecraft's <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/94/88/13/948813a63326f28df005d6960b98e90b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Gugs</a>*. I as an ST would go for maximum variety and probably use both animals and the eldritch horror version in my games, though local ferae might be more familiar and less prone to confusing the different critters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *No idea if Kadath would exist in the amazonian jungle, don't think so, but who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-24-2015, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:05:30-07:00","id":607469,"title":"","content":"So one of my players wants to use the Rite &quot;Enchant the Forest&quot; from page 205 in the core on the entire Amazon Rain Forest. The theory is the rite should be doable (if it has to be done several times) and it should be able to weaken Pentex in a major way as it would stop technology from working and make it so humans won't want to work or stay there. He feels the only thing that has really stopped the rite is the rarity of the items, and if it could be solved then there would be no problem and it would solve the War of the Amazon....yet to me it feels too easy...thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:59:25-07:00","id":607490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenrec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=607469#post607469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my players wants to use the Rite &quot;Enchant the Forest&quot; from page 205 in the core on the entire Amazon Rain Forest. The theory is the rite should be doable (if it has to be done several times) and it should be able to weaken Pentex in a major way as it would stop technology from working and make it so humans won't want to work or stay there. He feels the only thing that has really stopped the rite is the rarity of the items, and if it could be solved then there would be no problem and it would solve the War of the Amazon....yet to me it feels too easy...thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enchant the Forest is a bit too subtle to just shut everything down, and disrupting it by just showing up and cutting shit up with fomori probably qualifies as a disruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T00:13:11-07:00","id":607536,"title":"","content":"Pentex is building some sort of resort out in the jungle that bills itself as a &quot;Jungle adventure&quot;, however it is a completely &quot;Safe&quot; experience. The local natives are either replaced with actors or &quot;Tamed&quot;, local wild life is fake or used for hunting. Think of the Disney Jungle ride on steroids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T02:23:09-07:00","id":607560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=565069#post565069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were places where the Wyrm festered. The Mound Builders who were once the kin of the Croatan fell to corruption and had to be purged. There might be other examples (blood sorcerery influenced by vampires among the Aztecs) but my memory banks are too faulty.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there were vampires within MesoAmerican cultures as well as Mages. The other Changing Breeds however also were highly influential. Going South into South America this is the stronghold of the Balam and Mokole and conflict between Garou, Balam and Mokole is a very good starting point for any Amazon chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:54:54-07:00","id":609750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenrec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528134-amazon-and-pentex-ideas?p=607469#post607469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my players wants to use the Rite &quot;Enchant the Forest&quot; from page 205 in the core on the entire Amazon Rain Forest. The theory is the rite should be doable (if it has to be done several times) and it should be able to weaken Pentex in a major way as it would stop technology from working and make it so humans won't want to work or stay there. He feels the only thing that has really stopped the rite is the rarity of the items, and if it could be solved then there would be no problem and it would solve the War of the Amazon....yet to me it feels too easy...thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, tecnicaly he would be affecting a LOT of things if you let this be. It Depends on how you considers the limits of a forest and of the rite, but if you allow that, he will be affecting villages, cities and a lot of other things all across the forest.<br /> <br /> The Amazon isn't teeming just with animals. It is teeming with humans. Natives live all across the rain forest. There are cities of considerable size, technicaly inside the forest. Numerous scientific speditions work there. Numerous important economic activities occur in the forest, most of them AREN'T illegal woodcut. He'll be turning unlivable a portion of land almost the size of Europe, and if not as much populated, also far from unpopulated.<br /> <br /> I think it will be such a huge mess, so awesomely cathastrophic, that on second tought, I would simply let him do this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}